Subject: pci_host_generic: Ampere Altra ECAM quirk, 32-bit config reads only
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
Applies to: sys/dev/pci (pci_host_generic*, new pci_host_generic_quirks.h),
tests/sys/pci (new ATF test), etc/mtree/BSD.tests.dist, tests/sys/Makefile.
Needed on: Ampere Altra hosts (ACPI MCFG OEM ID "Ampere", OEM table ID
"Altra", OEM revision 1).  No tunable; inert on every other MCFG.

On the Altra, 8- and 16-bit PCI configuration reads can return wrong data
(a GPU's PCIe switch read as device 0, class 0), so devices go missing or
show the wrong IDs and drivers do not attach.  With the quirk every config
read is an aligned 32-bit read and the wanted bytes are extracted.  The
MCFG OEM quirk table moves to a header of pure helpers, which the new
tests/sys/pci/pci_host_generic_quirks_test exercises.  The existing
Marvell DesignWare entries are unchanged.  See kernel-patches/README.md.

